commit b0f2168e3e94e318d4f2cdc98ec26151b30831f8
Author: bench-agent <bench-agent@localhost>
Date:   Mon Oct 19 08:22:02 2026 +0200

    refactor(erc1155): name the error type in public trait impls

    With the `export-abi` feature the SDK 0.10 `#[public]` macro generates the
    Solidity interface printer for a trait impl on a separate marker struct, where
    `Self::Error` does not resolve and the crate fails to compile. Spell the
    associated error type out in the `IErc1155` and `IErc1155Burnable` impls.
    The types are the same, so neither the Rust API nor the ABI changes.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

